🟠 broker in messaging (prod-eu-1) keeps crashing because volume claim broker-log is out of space. It fails with "FATAL: log segment append failed: /data/segments/000042.log: No space left on device". Its last run lasted 10s; 2 restarts in the 1h4m since its pod was created. Fix in: persistentvolumeclaim/broker-log → spec.resources.requests.storage (8Gi). To check the size and capacity of the full volume claim, run kubectl describe pvc broker-log -n messaging
🟠 broker in messaging (prod-eu-1) keeps crashing because volume claim broker-log is out of space.
| 🟠 **broker** in **messaging** (**prod-eu-1**) keeps crashing because volume claim **broker-log** is out of space.
| It fails with
| ```
| FATAL: log segment append failed: /data/segments/000042.log: No space left on device
| ```
| Its last run lasted 10s; 2 restarts in the 1h4m since its pod was created.
| Fix in: persistentvolumeclaim/broker-log → spec.resources.requests.storage (8Gi).
| To check the size and capacity of the full volume claim, run
| ```
| kubectl describe pvc broker-log -n messaging
| ```
